    <!--
        THE MATERIALS A CASE CONSUMES, and what they cost.

        Where the rates come from
        *PRODUCTION DETAILS.xlsx* costs every product twice over: it states a
        purchase rate ("2800 a bottle") and, separately, a rupee figure per
        crown ("10.33"). The two do not always agree, and the sheet's own
        totals are built from the per-crown figures - the Ceramic block adds up
        to 416.821 exactly, to the third decimal, using them.

        So the per-crown figure is taken as the lab's truth, and the rate here
        is derived from it and the stated quantity. Two places where that
        matters:

        * Base dentine is priced per 50 g, not the 25 g the sheet's note says.
          2800/50 x 0.183 = 10.25, which is their 10.33; 2800/25 would be 20.5,
          which is nothing they have ever written down. The store's own
          purchase items are 50 g bottles, so the note is the error.
        * Investment is stated at 6700/kg, which for the 400 g per 30 units
          the same line gives would be 89.33 a unit, not the 0.60 they total.
          0.045/g is what their own figure implies; the stated rate is wrong by
          a factor of 150 and the lab should be told.

        Quantities in the bills of materials are rounded to two decimals,
        because that is this database's precision for quantities. The loss is
        under a rupee on a 143 rupee material cost, and raising a global
        setting for it would put three decimals on every quantity in the lab.

        Units
        Powders in grams, liquids in millilitres, everything countable in
        units, because that is what the sheet measures them in. Existing
        purchase items in the store are labelled BOTTLE or BOX with no
        conversion behind them (a legacy of the Odoo 17 data), which is why
        these are separate records: a bill of materials cannot consume 0.183 of
        a thing whose size nobody recorded. Each one names the purchase items
        it stands for.

        noupdate: a rate the lab corrects must survive an upgrade. (2026-09-25)
    -->
    <data noupdate="1">

